@page "/"
<PageTitle>Welcome</PageTitle>
<div class="container my-5">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-12 text-center">
            <h1 class="display-4">Kmila-9s: A Multiplatform VHDL Learning and Debugging Tool</h1>
            <p class="lead">
                An application for learning and debugging VHDL code without requiring physical hardware.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row mt-5">
        <div class="col-md-8 offset-md-2">
            <h2>Overview</h2>
            <p>
                Kmila-9s is a multiplatform desktop application, running in a local environment, aimed at debugging VHDL (VHSIC Hardware Description Language) code. Its objective is to facilitate the analysis of programs through simulation and interactive visualization of digital signals, clock cycles, and port states.
            </p>
            <p>
                The project aims to support the academic learning of digital design for FPGAs (Field Programmable Gate Arrays), offering a free and open-source tool that strengthens educational practices and allows for a practical understanding of the logic of digital systems without requiring physical hardware.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row mt-5">
        <div class="col-md-8 offset-md-2">
            <h2>Key Features</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Dynamic Variable Visualization:</strong> Observe the states of signals, ports, and internal variables at any time.</li>
                <li><strong>Cross-Platform:</strong> Runs on Windows, macOS, Android, iOS, iPadOS, and Linux (via web).</li>
                <li><strong>Standalone and Offline:</strong> Works locally without an internet connection.</li>
                <li><strong>"Pre-Laboratory" Function:</strong> Prepare for physical lab sessions in advance.</li>
                <li><strong>Accessibility:</strong> Study from any computer or mobile device.</li>
                <li><strong>Rapid Prototyping:</strong> Validate designs faster than with traditional methods.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row mt-5">
        <div class="col-12 text-center">
            <a href="/projects" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Go to Projects</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row mt-5">
        <div class="col-12 text-center">
            <p>
                Find more about the project on our
                <a href="https://github.com/Kmila9s" target="_blank">GitHub repository</a>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>